  "family": "chrome",
  "description": "Request header names, case and order that Chrome for Testing 153.0.8010.12 (Linux, --headless=new) sends, per request kind. Captured on loopback against a local logging server (HTTP/1.1 raw bytes, HTTPS h2 decoded). See docs/adr/0011-per-destination-headers.md and captures/chrome_153_linux.jsonl. Client hints after Accept-CH / Critical-CH: captures/chrome_153_linux_accept_ch.jsonl (tools/header_capture/accept_ch.js). Form POST navigations (the *_post lists): captures/chrome_153_linux_forms.jsonl (tests/header-capture/); captured without Accept-CH, so they have no high-entropy hint slots.",

  "browser_version": "153.0.8010.12",
  "captured": "2026-11-03",

  "syntax": [
    "Each request kind is a list of header slots in h2 wire order (names lowercase).",
    "\"name\" = value computed from the persona or the request (user-agent, sec-ch-ua*, accept-language, host, referer, origin, cookie, content-length, sec-fetch-site, sec-fetch-mode, sec-fetch-user, access-control-request-*). A slot with no value is skipped.",
    "\"name: value\" = fixed value.",
    "\"content-type\" = the Content-Type the request carries (form enctype); skipped when there is none.",
    "*_post lists: form POST navigations; *_post_redirect: their redirect hops (303 turns them into GET, so content-length, content-type and origin drop out; 307/308 keep them).",
    "\"@group\" = the renderer header group: user-agent, sec-ch-ua*, accept-language and the page's own headers, in Blink's hash-table order (see renderer_group).",
    "HTTP/1.1 = the same list with `host` and `connection: keep-alive` in front and `priority` removed, names re-cased by h1.",
    "\"sec-ch-ua-arch\", \"sec-ch-ua-platform-version\", ... (the high-entropy hints) are computed slots sent only when the origin asked for them with Accept-CH (lb_net::client_hints). document_restart is the Critical-CH retry of a navigation; captures/chrome_153_linux_accept_ch.jsonl is the evidence."
  ],

  "h1": {
    "prefix": ["host", "connection: keep-alive"],
    "drop": ["priority"],
    "lowercase_prefixes": ["sec-ch-"],
    "note": "Every other name is Title-Case (Accept-Language, Sec-Fetch-Site, ...). Names the page sets itself keep the case the page gave."
  },

